      "title": "The whole group policy ends",
      "narration": "Now change the facts. The employer's entire group policy ends, or a covered class is removed, instead of Marcus simply leaving his job. A separate Maryland provision addresses this event. It protects an insured who has been covered for at least five years before termination, subject to the conversion conditions. The policy may limit the individual amount to the lesser of the lost coverage after the specified new-group offset, or ten thousand dollars. Do not apply this five-year requirement and possible cap to every ordinary employment-termination conversion question.",
